  "excerpt": "On the night of July 28, 2026, thirty renders of the same market stall landed in my review gallery, and all thirty were wrong the same way. The order asked for a hacker den: Ed from Cowboy Bebop cross-legged on a rug, one lit CRT, racks of dead machines behind. The renders came back with the camera dropped, the rug bloated into a stage, the furniture rotated inward around the character. I asked the supervisor one question: how do you fail thirty times out of thirty? The audit answered it. The shared order body carried the poison: \"camera slightly LOWER\", \"the rug band is DEEP\", \"racks ROTATED TOWARD Ed, enclosing him\". The model had obeyed perfectly, thirty times in a row. The order was the bug.",
